TEXT 768 536 Left 1 ;time to reach comp threshold: t (set in project cosntraints)\nthreshold voltage for comp: V_th (to compute)\ncurrent mirror ratio: k = 0.1 (10:1)\n \nt = ( C * V_th ) / ( k * Iref )     => pulse width is directly inversely proportional to Iref!\n \nif we take t=4.5us for Iref=1uA, we can use a V_th=1.65V as it's\nthe switching point of an inverter, we get then a C/k ratio of 2.727pF\nif we keep our k=0.1 we can then know we need to use a 272.7fF cap value\n \n \n\n \n\n \n??? BUT it's 1.4x slower than supposed to, so lets use 272.7fF/1.4 = 194.8fF ??
